{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/958193-a-mechanical-discussion-of-praxes","id":958193,"title":"A Mechanical Discussion of Praxes","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-08-26T06:36:02-07:00","id":958193,"title":"A Mechanical Discussion of Praxes","content":"Just wanted to start a discussion collecting people's thoughts on what makes a good Praxis, speaking strictly from a mechanical perspective. Basically, what types of spells benefit the most from being able to score an exceptional success roughly 16% of the time (on 5 dice) vs. roughly .25% of the time?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12307-frishman","name":"Frishman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-26T07:10:59-07:00","id":958211,"title":"","content":"Anything that is all-or-nothing based on Withstand, for one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-26T07:15:02-07:00","id":958215,"title":"","content":"Spells that you have 9+ dice to normally cast (Gnosis 3, Arcana 4, Shadow Name 2 can get you there. Movers and shakers, not initiates), or spells that you cast all the time. Preferably both. The two big reasons to want exceptional successes are to apply conditions and generate beats (in which case spells you cast the most often should be praxes) or to apply the ignore withstand option (in which case it should be your most versatile spell that has the highest withstand normally). Rewrite Time, the adept Time spell, is going to hit withstand of the target's resolve or the temporal withstanding from what you want to change, whichever is higher, plus 2 because there are multiple withstand ratings. That's a good one to want to ignore withstand. The Mind initiate spell Know Nature can be used on everyone you meet, and is beneficial to you to cast on everyone. That is a good one to want to gain condition generating beats. If your legacy has an attainment that you can take as a praxis before joining that meets these qualifications, it is even better.<br /> <br /> I picked my Praxes based off roleplay, though. They are spells that my character would have first learned to delve into certain Arcana, but they fall into the &quot;condition generating&quot; category since she casts them all the time. It is kind of circular reasoning, she casts them all the time because they are her praxes, but the RP is that they are praxes because she casts them all the time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11862-ifisa","name":"Ifisa","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-26T07:36:39-07:00","id":958224,"title":"","content":"My mastigos took co-location as a praxis to give the opportunity to refund the mana spent on casting it sympathetically. He has gnosis 2 and Space 3 right now, so he will typically add in high speech and his dedicated tool (both for the yantra and to mitigate paradox). He also has the anti-poison spell in Life (can't remember the name of it off the top of my head) just so that if he needs it he won't have to spend mana on it.<br /> <br /> But yeah, Ifisa has the more standard answer. Positive conditions are great to generate beats off of, so that's a big reason to take a praxis (far larger than any willpower or mana refund imho). Bypassing withstand is definitely something you will want to do when combat comes up. Of course if it's an offensive spell a rote is just as practical. And as Ifisa said, don't ignore role play value as well. Both rotes and praxi (? what is the multiple of praxis) will be spells that you will want to cast a lot for the benefits available from them. It's a very mage thing to have a go to spell(s).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","name":"Falcon777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-26T10:43:44-07:00","id":958285,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Falcon777</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/958193-a-mechanical-discussion-of-praxes?p=958224#post958224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">He has gnosis 2 and Space 3 right now, so he will typically add in high speech and his dedicated tool (both for the yantra and to mitigate paradox).</div> </div> </div> </div>Would the paradox mitigation count as a separate Yantra or do you just get it whenever you use a Dedicated Tool as a Yantra?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2273,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2273-incendax","user":"Incendax","date":".  Confusing wording. 08-27-2016, 07:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2273-incendax","name":"Incendax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-26T11:38:22-07:00","id":958314,"title":"","content":"He only mentioned 2, High Speech and Dedicated Tool, mitigating Paradox is just an additional benefit of using your Dedicated Tool whether or not it's providing dice when you use it as a Yantra.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-26T11:52:23-07:00","id":958319,"title":"","content":"Do you still enjoy Paradox mitigation when using your Dedicated Tool as an appropriate Yantra, or is it one or the other?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-26T12:29:33-07:00","id":958348,"title":"","content":"Like I just said, if you use your Dedicated Tool as a Yantra it mitigates Paradox.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-26T13:21:29-07:00","id":958382,"title":"","content":"As the counter to that, if you are <i>not</i> using your Dedicated Tool as a Yantra, you do <i>not</i> get the Paradox mitigation. Hence why so many Mages use their D-Tool in everything they can get away with.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, thank you all for your input in this. I honestly hadn't considered the Condition-spam benefits. I'm not used to the new Beat system, last game I played was Changeling several years back.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12307-frishman","name":"Frishman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}